      "content": "That makes sense. We're also seeing some cases where the pigmentation is really bizarre—like deep, dark, almost muddy splotches that seem to have this strange, mottled, or even \"stunted\" appearance compared to normal melanocyte distribution. For cases where the visual presentation is just fundamentally \"off\" or looks somewhat primitive or irregular compared to typical dermatological patterns, is there a specific sub-category we should be looking at to capture that anomalous appearance, or is it strictly a matter of falling back to the L-series unspecified codes?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
